<BaseLayout title="The Fulton County Court Order | Who Is Abebe?">

  <Header>
    <Fragment slot="title">The Fulton County Court Order</Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      Dossier 2.0 · New October 2026.
      An order in Abebe Caesar Ventures, LLC v. Mekonnen Abebe and three
      other companies, Superior Court of Fulton County, Civil Action File
      No. 26CV006560.
    </Fragment>
  </Header>

  <main class="article-wrap">
    <article class="article-body report-page">

      <p class="lede">
        In May 2026 a Fulton County judge ordered Mekonnen Abebe and three
        Abebe companies to transfer their interest in certain properties to
        Abebe Caesar Ventures, LLC, the company named as owner on the Sylvan
        Road rezoning. This page sets out what the order says, what each side
        told the court, and what is still open. It draws no conclusion.
      </p>

      <div class="notice-box">
        <strong>Scope:</strong>
        Everything below comes from a six-page copy of the order. The copy
        carries the stamp "Fulton County Superior Court ***EFILED***" with the
        date "5/29/2026 4:33 PM" and the Clerk's name. This site did not
        retrieve it from the court's online portal, which refuses automated
        requests. The case number can be checked with the Clerk of Superior
        Court of Fulton County. The copy is posted here unaltered:
        <a href="/docs/court/fulton-26CV006560-order-granting-interlocutory-injunction.pdf">Order Granting Interlocutory Injunction (PDF, 6 pages)</a>. This is an order on emergency motions. It is
        not a final judgment. The order says: "This order does not finally
        resolve any matter that the parties otherwise have the right to bring
        to arbitration under the terms of the operating agreement." The
        complaint, the motions and the operating agreement were not read.
      </div>

